Z||000001||AkursedX||07-28-2001||08:57 PM||||Well hopefully Grinthock will fill you in on this.  He knows alot about it.  <P>But from what I understand is that you can't get satellite TV in Canada because they don't offer it there.  So how can you steal something you can't buy??  <P>But I'm not 100% sure on my info.<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||72vinman||07-28-2001||09:11 PM||||They consider the use of American satelite providers as a grey market as opposed to the black market. As Akursedx said you can't steal what is not available to purchase. However, there are Canadian satelite providers as well and from what I understand they are trying to use pirated cards for it. That is a no-no, totally illegal. You can get a US directv system for under $400 Cdn. Trust me it has a lot of channels to waste the time away with. Just check in any newspaper classified there are a ton of companies out there right now. Good Luck||||reg||10
